family: web-ui
what: trap
transport: v3
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: RFC 3416 (SNMPv2 notifications), RFC 3414 (SNMPv3 users)
does: The values to enter in the device's SNMP trap (notification) page so it sends traps to Woodshed (SNMPv3).
check: Search Events for type Traps after saving; pages with a "send test trap" button send one at once.
placeholders: <V3-USER> <AUTH-PASSPHRASE> <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Add the same user in Woodshed: Settings → SNMP → v3 users, with the same name, protocols and passphrases.
- Field names differ between devices. Many pages also ask which events send a trap.
---- part steps "": In the device's web page, open its SNMP trap or notification settings and add a receiver
Trap receiver (manager) address: 192.0.2.10
Port: 162
SNMP version: v3
User name: <V3-USER>
Security level: authentication and privacy (authPriv)
Authentication: SHA-256, passphrase <AUTH-PASSPHRASE>
Privacy: AES-128, passphrase <PRIV-PASSPHRASE>
Notification type: trap (not inform), unless the page offers informs and you want them answered
==== text
